{"title":"Topicwise Test-3 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Algorithms -1","fileName":"083_Topicwise Test-3 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Algorithms -1.html","branch":"COMPUTER SCIENCE ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 GATE 2025 Online Test Series Computer Science Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In an array of <em>n</em> elements, the elements increase from the beginning until the peak element and then they start to decrease till the last element. Find the time complexity of the most efficient algorithm which finds the peak element.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/a3f61f584717e5b0f86edc42c682c531b6e77c81.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/644910cf5f5d49900b017f1bacb0a8caafd20778.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/51e96150df000ce8acf8d6146585641cbf394a42.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/da8f1b348cb78ff7052a7794013753a6d2c83db0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/23df96a243e73f9ca86f5d62d70588ba6b1fd12b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>There are n unsorted arrays: <em>A</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>A</em><sub>2</sub>, ..... <em>A<sub>n</sub></em>. Assume that n is odd. Each of <em>A</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>A</em><sub>2</sub>, ..... <em>A</em><sub>n</sub> contains n distinct elements. There are no common elements between any two arrays. The worst-case time complexity of computing the median of the medians of <em>A</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>A</em><sub>2</sub>, ..... <em>A</em><sub>n</sub> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Ο(n)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"